--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52841-talismans-and-sekhem-ratings?p=52864#post52864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was what I gathered, yes. Except they're effectively at 10 sekhem unless someone yoinked their talisman.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the benefits are <i>totally</i> worth it. An invincible extra respawn point? Yes, please!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:32:21-08:00","id":54751,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the one thing I don't get about them is how the entry makes it seem like stealing talismans is <i>common</i>. Like...how is that a problem that <i>doesn't</i> immediately solve itself? &quot;Oh, someone has stolen my talisman. I guess I'd better spawn <i>on top of them</i> next descent. Or right now. Whatever&quot; You'd think, like, the second time a mummy materialized out of thin air and threw you through a wall, you'd pretty much put all the talismans down and walk away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 01-21-2014, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T12:52:32-08:00","id":54838,"title":"","content":"I think the rules are there just in case. To show why some crazy person might even try to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T13:36:09-08:00","id":54869,"title":"","content":"And you do kind of have to <i>kill yourself</i> to make it work, which isn't a great experience however you look at it. And yeah, Mummy's full of things that are terrible ideas if you know what's going to happen to you when you do them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T16:49:15-08:00","id":55034,"title":"","content":"It's mostly the way the rules are written, with limits on how many a mummy can use at once and so forth, that made it seem like yoinking a couple extra talismans was in some way a common practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T17:30:49-08:00","id":55057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52841-talismans-and-sekhem-ratings?p=55034#post55034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly the way the rules are written, with limits on how many a mummy can use at once and so forth, that made it seem like yoinking a couple extra talismans was in some way a common practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading was that it was pretty common for Mummies to turn over their Talismans to other members of their Guild, especially to their masters or other superiors. A Guildmaster with a bunch of Talismans from his subordinates is crazy powerful. As for his subordinates, they're slightly less powerful and their Descents are a little shorter, but they have an extremely powerful superior with a vested interest in their continued well-being holding on to a &quot;spirit organ&quot; that they can reclaim whenever things go badly for them. Seems like a pretty great deal, especially if their master rotates <i>his</i> Talisman through his subordinates, gaining a similar security benefit and boosting <i>their</i> power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:14:09-08:00","id":55082,"title":"","content":"I suppose that depends on the level of trust between Arisen of a given Guild in a given Nome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:29:14-08:00","id":55544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52841-talismans-and-sekhem-ratings?p=55082#post55082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose that depends on the level of trust between Arisen of a given Guild in a given Nome.</div> </div> </div> </div>How's trust come into it? If someone betrays you and makes off with your Talisman, it's pretty easy to visit unholy devastation on them or otherwise get it back. Even if you don't want to suicide-jack it, you can still probably benefit from &quot;Entombed or Nearby&quot; when making Kepher rolls. And you'd better have at least a working relationship with the masters of your Guild, as they're your main source of new Utterances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:18:59-08:00","id":55569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egarwaen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52841-talismans-and-sekhem-ratings?p=55544#post55544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How's trust come into it? If someone betrays you and makes off with your Talisman, it's pretty easy to visit unholy devastation on them or otherwise get it back. Even if you don't want to suicide-jack it, you can still probably benefit from &quot;Entombed or Nearby&quot; when making Kepher rolls. And you'd better have at least a working relationship with the masters of your Guild, as they're your main source of new Utterances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because suicide is a Memory 2 violation and most mummies don't want to resort to that no matter how pragmatic it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}